So d divides 9d - 56. Since d divides 9d, d must divide 56.

So d = b + 7 is a positive divisor of 56. Also b > 9, so d = b + 7 > 16. Divisors of 56 greater than 16: 28, 56. (Also 14? 14 is not >16. 7,8,14,28,56. So 28 and 56.)

Check d = 28: b = 21. Then 17_b = 28, 97_b = 9*21 + 7 = 189 + 7 = 196. 196 / 28 = 7. Yes, 28 divides 196.

Check d = 56: b = 49. Then 17_b = 56, 97_b = 9*49 + 7 = 441 + 7 = 448. 448 / 56 = 8. Yes, 56 divides 448.

Are there any other divisors? d must be > 16. Divisors of 56: 1,2,4,7,8,14,28,56. Only 28 and 56 are >16. So b = 21 and b = 49.

Sum of all integer bases b > 9: 21 + 49 = 70.

