[26/92] SuperGPQA/Science Evaluate the definite integral of the absolute logarithm
We need to evaluate the definite integral from 1/e to e of |ln x| dx.

Let's compute.

The function ln x is negative for x < 1 and positive for x > 1. The interval [1/e, e] includes x from 1/e to 1 (where ln x < 0) and from 1 to e (where ln x > 0). So |ln x| = -ln x for x in [1/e, 1], and ln x for x in [1, e].

